# clause-syntax — Design

Parser + AST construction phase. Consumes a TokenStream from
clause-lex, produces a concrete syntax tree. Emits syntax-level
diagnostics.

## Scope

- G0 grammar primitives: Cursor, Stream, NodeBuilder, error-recovery
  scaffolding. Hosted here (rather than clause-ir) because they're
  parser-specific.
- Concrete AST node types — one per grammar production.
- `Parser` — drives token consumption, builds AST.
- `AstArena` — const-sized node storage (arvo-style stack-only;
  arena size is a const generic chosen by the caller).
- Syntax diagnostics via clause-ir::Diagnostic.
- Error recovery: parser can synchronise at statement boundaries
  and continue parsing — multiple errors per invocation.

## Non-scope

- Name binding / scope resolution (clause-resolve).
- Type checking (clause-typecheck).
- AST rewriting / macros (separate round post-core).

## Dependencies

- `clause-ir` for Span / NodeId / AstNodeKind / Diagnostic.
- `clause-lex` for Token + TokenStream.
- arvo for USize / Cap / newtype discipline.
- `#![no_std]`, no alloc. AST arena is const-generic.

## Provisional module layout

- `parser.rs` — top-level Parser + drive loop.
- `grammar/` — one file per grammar production (expr, stmt, item,
  type, pattern, etc.).
- `ast.rs` — concrete AST node structs.
- `arena.rs` — const-sized NodeArena.
- `framework.rs` — G0 primitives (Cursor, Stream, NodeBuilder).
- `diagnostics.rs` — syntax error construction.

